final_text:
No behavioural regression found: the refactor is behaviour-preserving, and `go vet ./internal/` plus `go test ./internal/ -count=1` pass offline (live provider tests skip, Dockerfile not built). The findings below are defects carried into the extracted helpers and cleanup the PR left behind, ranked most severe first.

```json
[
  {
    "file": "internal/backup.go",
    "line": 360,
    "summary": "checkJustTokenProvider counts every non-empty auth parameter, so for Gitea and Sourcehut (whose enabledProviderAuth entries are API URL + token) an API URL alone counts as a configured provider, contradicting checkProvider's documented '0 or 1' return.",
    "failure_scenario": "Set GIT_BACKUP_DIR and GITEA_APIURL (or SOURCEHUT_APIURL) with no token: checkProvidersDefined gets count=1 and returns nil instead of 'no providers defined'. collectProviderBackupResults gates on the token, so nothing runs; the run logs 'all backups failed' with 0/0, exits 0 in one-shot mode, and under SOBA_NOTIFY_ON_FAILURE_ONLY the notification is skipped as 'no failures'."
  },
  {
    "file": "internal/backup.go",
    "line": 277,
    "summary": "displayBitBucketStartupConfig still gates only on BITBUCKET_EMAIL, although this PR adds bitbucketAPITokenDefined/bitbucketOAuthDefined, which are the predicates that actually decide whether BitBucket runs.",
    "failure_scenario": "OAuth2-only setup (BITBUCKET_USER/KEY/SECRET, no email): the backup runs but no 'BitBucket backups to keep / compare method / backup LFS' lines are logged at startup. Conversely, email set without an API token logs BitBucket config for a provider that will not run."
  },
  {
    "file": "internal/backup.go",
    "line": 219,
    "summary": "The new shared log helpers read settings via GetEnvOrFile (honouring *_FILE), but the providers read the same settings with os.Getenv only, so the startup banner can report configuration that is not in effect.",
    "failure_scenario": "GITHUB_COMPARE_FILE points at a file containing 'refs': startup logs 'GitHub compare method: refs', but github.go passes os.Getenv(envGitHubCompare) == \"\" and the backup uses clone comparison. Same mismatch for logProviderOrgs (line 204, vs getOrgsListFromEnvVar) and logProviderBackupsToKeep (line 211, vs getEnvIntDefault)."
  },
  {
    "file": "internal/backup.go",
    "line": 689,
    "summary": "checkProvidersDefined intercepts both BitBucket providers in the switch, so they never reach checkProvider/checkUserAndPasswordProvider; partial BitBucket credentials produce no 'parameter is not defined' error, and the BitBucket entries in userAndPasswordProviders are dead.",
    "failure_scenario": "GITHUB_TOKEN set, BITBUCKET_EMAIL set, BITBUCKET_API_TOKEN missing or misspelt: validation passes and BitBucket is silently never backed up, whereas the equivalent Azure DevOps partial config (username without PAT) fails startup with 'provider configuration invalid'. The helpers also use != \"\" where checkProvider uses strings.Trim, so a whitespace-only token counts as complete."
  },
  {
    "file": "internal/backup.go",
    "line": 495,
    "summary": "scheduleBackups still builds a gocron scheduler before the switch, so the one-shot path and the NewJob-error path create a scheduler that is never used or shut down, even though the new runScheduledJob helper is the natural owner.",
    "failure_scenario": "With no interval or cron set, every Run() allocates a scheduler it never starts or shuts down (tests call Run() repeatedly in one process). With an invalid GIT_BACKUP_CRON, runScheduledJob returns 'failed to create job' without calling s.Shutdown(). Creating the scheduler inside runScheduledJob with a deferred Shutdown removes both."
  },
  {
    "file": "internal/backup.go",
    "line": 228,
    "summary": "logProviderBackupLFS (and the skip-user-repos check at line 240) calls GetEnvOrFile only for its 'exists' flag and then envTrue, which reads os.Getenv only, so the GetEnvOrFile call is redundant.",
    "failure_scenario": "'exists && envTrue(envVar)' always equals 'envTrue(envVar)'. When only GITHUB_BACKUP_LFS_FILE is set, the extra call opens and reads the file (or logs 'file ... does not exist') on every startup for a value that can never enable the flag. The helper reduces to 'if envTrue(envVar)'."
  },
  {
    "file": "docker/Dockerfile",
    "line": 8,
    "summary": "The rewritten RUN instruction keeps 'rm -f \"/var/cache/apk/*\"', where the quoted glob is never expanded, so the cleanup is a no-op and is redundant with 'apk add --no-cache' anyway.",
    "failure_scenario": "The shell passes the literal path '/var/cache/apk/*' to rm, and -f hides the miss, so nothing is removed. The Dockerfile clean-up pass touched this instruction but left a dead command that looks like it trims the layer; drop it or unquote the glob."
  },
  {
    "file": "internal/backup_test.go",
    "line": 629,
    "summary": "After extracting the assertion helpers, each switch arm in TestGiteaOrgsRepositoryBackup still calls resetBackups() and is then followed by an unconditional resetBackups() at the end of the loop body.",
    "failure_scenario": "The backup directory is wiped twice per iteration; the per-arm calls (lines 629 and 632) are dead duplication. Keeping only the trailing resetBackups() gives the same behaviour and removes the residue the complexity refactor was meant to clear."
  },
  {
    "file": "internal/notify.go",
    "line": 27,
    "summary": "The extracted titleBackupsErrors and titleBackupsFailed constants begin with a stray U+FE0F variation selector (bytes ef b8 8f) before the emoji, copied verbatim from the old literals.",
    "failure_scenario": "Every 'completed with errors' and 'failed' title sent to the ntfy Title header, Slack and Telegram starts with an orphan invisible code point, while the success title does not; exact-match filters or alert rules on the title text will miss. Centralising the literals was the point to drop it."
  },
  {
    "file": "internal/backup.go",
    "line": 205,
    "summary": "The new shared logProviderOrgs helper bakes in the misspelling 'Organistations' for all providers, and displayGitLabStartupConfig passes the label 'Gitlab' to logProviderBackupLFS while using 'GitLab' for its other lines.",
    "failure_scenario": "Startup logs print 'GitHub Organistations: ...' and mix 'GitLab compare method' with 'Gitlab backup LFS: true' (line 273), so grepping logs for 'Organisations' or 'GitLab' misses lines. The redundant strings.ToLower(orgs) != \"\" check and double ToLower are also carried over."
  }
]
```
